-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Ray Parallel to Frame:** If $\mathbf{d}_{cam}[a] \approx 0$, the ray is parallel to the boundary. The intersection $t$ is infinity. This is handled by the validity mask [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-- **Origin at Camera:** If the origin is at the camera position (norm $< \epsilon$) and near is $t=0$, the ray is valid. If the origin is not at the camera but depth is near zero, it is marked invalid [S2, unofficial].
-- **Infinite Far:** If far is $t=\infty$, the projection is at infinity. The $xy$ coordinates are not well-defined, but the $t$ value is used for bounding [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
